onary.\n\nERP (POL-RD-09): The SGD 5.50 of CTE ERP is ALREADY COMPREHENDED inside the 10.72/10.75 refund, because the recomputed fare credits only on-optimal-route gantries and the optimal Thomson Road routing carries 0.00 ERP. Under POL-RD-09(1) it is itemised for transparency but is never added on top. Both gantries are matched to the trace within the 250 m radius (nearest fixes 0.0 m at 08:40:55 and 24.1 m at 08:52:45), so there is no phantom line, no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral and no POL-RD-10(8) escalation.\n\nNo POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifiers all match TRP-00106, the trace is unimpaired, the refund is well under the SGD 150.00 ceiling and under charged_total, no exculpatory clause was invoked against a missing artifact, and every charge line has a counterpart in the trace or trip record. Two rider claims that cited the missing advisory without disclosing its impairment and issue code were discarded by the referee; they are recorded in the audit and are not relied on. Confidence is set at 0.90, the deciding facts being carried by weight-1.0 artifacts (gps_trace, trip_record, fare_breakdown)."
